{
	"info": {
		"name": "decidiq-participation-publication",
		"description": "Wire contract for the four endpoints gate-25 found had never been called by any automated test:\n\n  GET  /api/settings/publication-config                       settings#getPublicationConfig\n  PUT  /api/settings/publication-config                       settings#setPublicationConfig\n  POST /api/participation/proposals/{proposalId}/vote         participationBudget#castAdvisoryVote\n  POST /api/participation/budgets/{budgetId}/publish          participationBudget#publishBudgetResults\n\nWriting this collection is what found three product defects, all of which it now pins. Every one of them was a HEALTHY HTTP 200/201 with an empty or wrong body, so none of them was visible from a status code alone:\n\n  1. A citizen could vote on the same advisory proposal without limit. The dedup query filtered on `_relations.budget-proposal` — the schema SLUG — and OpenRegister keys its `_relations` JSONB by the property path it walked (`relations.0.id`), never by the slug. Zero rows, guard skipped, second CitizenVote written with the same 'idempotency' slug as the first.\n  2. The advisory tally wrote votesFor=0/votesAgainst=0 back over real votes, from the same broken filter.\n  3. publishBudgetResults published `proposals: []` / `participationCount: 0` / `allocatedAmount: 0` for every round, because fetchValidatedProposals filtered on `_relations.participatory-budget` instead of the flat `participatoryBudget` property the portal actually writes.\n\nSo the duplicate-vote request here asserts 409 and the publish request asserts a NON-EMPTY allocation. Both fail on the pre-fix tree — that is the point of them; a test that only asserted 2xx passed the whole time the feature was broken.\n\nSelf-contained and idempotent: seeds its own ParticipatoryBudget + BudgetProposal through OpenRegister's object API (ADR-022) and deletes them in teardown.",
		"schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
	},
	"variable": [
		{ "key": "baseUrl", "value": "http://localhost:8080" },
		{ "key": "noAuthBase", "value": "http://localhost:8080" },
		{ "key": "adminUser", "value": "admin" },
		{ "key": "adminPass", "value": "admin" },
		{ "key": "register", "value": "decidiq" },
		{ "key": "budgetId", "value": "" },
		{ "key": "proposalId", "value": "" },
		{ "key": "votingDeadline", "value": "" }
	],
	"item": [
		{
			"name": "Setup: compute a voting deadline 30 days out",
			"event": [
				{
					"listen": "prerequest",
					"script": {
						"type": "text/javascript",
						"exec": [
							"// budgetAcceptsVotes() requires status 'voting' AND a deadline strictly in",
							"// the future, so the fixture cannot carry a hardcoded date.",
							"const d = new Date(Date.now() + 30 * 24 * 60 * 60 * 1000);",
							"pm.collectionVariables.set('votingDeadline', d.toISOString().replace(/\\.\\d{3}Z$/, 'Z'));"
						]
					}
				},
				{
					"listen": "test",
					"script": {
						"type": "text/javascript",
						"exec": [
							"pm.test('Setup: health endpoint reachable (200)', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
							"pm.test('Setup: a future voting deadline was computed', () => {",
							"  const v = pm.collectionVariables.get('votingDeadline');",
							"  pm.expect(v, 'votingDeadline').to.be.a('string').and.to.have.length.above(0);",
							"  pm.expect(new Date(v).getTime()).to.be.above(Date.now());",
							"});"
						]
					}
				}
			],
			"request": {
				"auth": {
					"type": "basic",
					"basic": [
						{ "key": "username", "value": "{{adminUser}}", "type": "string" },
						{ "key": "password", "value": "{{adminPass}}", "type": "string" }
					]
				},
				"method": "GET",
				"header": [
					{ "key": "Accept", "value": "application/json" },
					{ "key": "OCS-APIRequest", "value": "true" }
				],
				"url": {
					"raw": "{{baseUrl}}/index.php/apps/decidiq/api/health",
					"host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
					"path": ["index.php", "apps", "decidiq", "api", "health"]
				}
			}
		},
